WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.260
Narrator: Imagine feeding your baby

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:05.230
a milkshake for every meal.

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:08.920
Well, for hooded seal
pups, that's nothing.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.060
Their mother's milk contains 60% fat,

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:14.730
the fattiest milk in the world.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:18.120
For comparison, the
richest ice cream clocks in

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.820
at only 16% fat.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.010
And after just three to five
days guzzling the stuff,

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:26.840
seal pups double their body weight.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.343
But seals aren't the only
animals with extreme milk.

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.700
If hooded seals drink the fattiest milk,

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.890
then tammar wallabies prefer
their milk loaded with sugar.

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:42.040
It can contain as much as 12% sugar,

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.160
more than a glass of
Coca-Cola, and for good reason.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.130
Joeys are born prematurely

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:51.120
and finish developing outside the womb.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.130
And since sugars are
easier to digest than fat,

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:58.330
their milk is easier on their
developing digestive systems.

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:01.060
Meanwhile, the milk also contains

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:04.910
an antibiotic more
powerful than penicillin,

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:06.680
which protects the young joeys

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.660
from germs since they're born

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:11.510
without a fully functioning immune system.

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:15.760
Meanwhile, aardvark milk
doesn't contain much sugar,

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.310
but it makes up for it with
extreme levels of protein.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:24.660
While cow's milk has a
measly 3 to 4% protein,

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:28.670
aardvark milk can contain over 13%,

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:32.600
making it among the
highest-protein milks on earth,

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.390
giving calves enough nutrition

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:36.900
to reach 30% of their adult weight

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.130
in just three months.

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:42.500
But while aardvarks have
some pretty potent milk,

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:47.340
nine-banded armadillos make
some special stuff of their own.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.880
By the time the pups are a
month old, they're drinking milk

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.980
that contains 10 times as
much calcium as cow's milk.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:57.510
All this calcium helps the pups develop

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:02.490
those famous armor shells,
which are actually made of bone.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.870
Next up, flamingos.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:07.310
That's right, flamingos.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:09.770
Like most birds, they feed their chicks

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:12.610
by vomiting directly into their mouths,

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:15.720
but that food isn't
made of the day's catch.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:20.130
Instead, it consists of a
substance called crop milk

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:22.760
because it's stored in the parent's crop,

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:25.690
and flamingos are one of only three birds

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:27.870
that can produce this stuff.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.150
But even among our feathered friends,

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:35.060
flamingo crop milk is
special because it's pink.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:36.800
That's because the pigments

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.100
that give flamingos their
brilliant coloring leach out

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.640
of their feathers and into the milk.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.810
Now, all this milk might sound

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:48.230
like the next health-food
craze, but there's a good reason

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:51.050
we generally stick to plain old cattle:

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:54.144
They're much easier to milk.

